{"name":"Pacific Queen","hex":"#026b5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pacific","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Calm, peaceful.","Preferring peace by nature; avoiding violence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pacific"},{"term":"queen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wife, consort, or widow of a king.","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act the part of a queen; to behave imperiously; to queen it.","To make a queen or (figuratively) to give the status of a queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balclutha (1886)","blocks":[{"text":"Balclutha, also known as Star of Alaska, Pacific Queen, or Sailing Ship Balclutha, is a steel-hulled full-rigged ship that was built in 1886. She is representative of several different commercial ventures, including lumber, salmon, and grain. She is a U.S. National Historic Landmark and is currently preserved as part of San Francisco Maritime National Historical Park in San Francisco, California, although temporarily on display in Vallejo. She was added to the National Register of Historic Places on 7 November 1976."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Balclutha_2016.jpg/330px-Balclutha_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balclutha_(1886)","wikidata":"Q804713"},{"title":"Pacific Ocean","blocks":[{"text":"The Pacific Ocean is the largest and deepest of Earth's five oceanic divisions. It stretches from the Arctic Ocean in the north to the Southern Ocean, or, depending on the definition, to Antarctica in the south, and is bounded by the continents of Asia and Australia in the west and the Americas in the east."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/Pacific_Ocean_-_en.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https:/